    "apply_url": "https://zebra.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/Zebra_careers/job/Bengaluru-India/Intern-II_JR103699",
    "description": "Overview:\nAt Zebra, we are a community of innovators who come together to create new ways of working. United by curiosity and a culture of caring, we develop smart solutions that anticipate our customer\u2019s and partner\u2019s needs and solve their challenges.\nBeing part of Zebra Nation means you are seen, heard, valued, and respected. Drawing from our unique perspectives, we collaborate to deliver on our purpose. Here you are part of a team pushing boundaries today to redefine the work of tomorrow for organizations, their employees, and those they serve.\nYou\u2019ll have opportunities to learn and lead in a forward-thinking environment, defining your path to a fulfilling career while channeling your skills toward causes you care about\u2014locally and globally.\nCome make an impact every day at Zebra.\nWhat We're Looking For:\nWe are seeking an enthusiastic and detail-oriented Software Intern to support building our Agentic AI systems. The ideal candidate should be innovative, forward-thinking to design, prototype, and build next-generation, AI-powered automation systems.\nYou will be at the forefront of engineering intelligence: building autonomous, agentic AI systems that optimize our CI/CD pipelines, automatically generate and run software tests, or leverage Natural Language Processing (NLP) to predict and replicate complex defect patterns across multi-product software platforms. You will own the project end-to-end: from initial architectural design and API integration to piloting the live AI systems in active engineering programs. Key Responsibilities:\n\u2022 Design and Architect AI Prototypes : Research, design, and implement end-to-end software prototypes leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs), Agentic workflows, and semantic similarity models.\n\u2022 Pipeline & Tool Integration : Connect internal engineering systems by writing robust APIs, script engines, and data connectors (integrating with tools such as Git/GitHub, Jira, CI/CD pipelines, and physical/virtual Device Farms).\n\u2022 Build Data & Parse Automation : Design algorithms to programmatically parse and analyze code-level build deltas (Git diffs, Abstract Syntax Trees) or semantic unstructured text data (Jira ticket descriptions, system logs).\n\u2022 Orchestration & Workflow Automation : Build autonomous execution loops that can trigger tests, evaluate results, auto-log issues, and generate real-time product/release health reports.\n\u2022 Measure & Harden for Production : Deploy the system in a \"shadow mode\" pilot alongside active engineering teams, capture performance/accuracy metrics, resolve false positives, and deliver a production-ready package with clean documentation.\nBenefits:\nWe understand the importance of work-life balance and wellbeing, which is why we offer flexibility for our teams including: hybrid work, adaptable hours, Summer Flex Fridays, Focus Fridays, and an annual companywide well-being day to promote revitalization and success.\nJob Posting Statement:\nTo protect candidates from falling victim to online fraudulent activity involving fake job postings and employment offers, please be aware our recruiters will always connect with you via @zebra.com email accounts. Applications are only accepted through our applicant tracking system and only accept personal identifying information through that system. Our Talent Acquisition team will not ask for you to provide personal identifying information via e-mail or outside of the system. If you are a victim of identity theft contact your local police department.\nAI Technology Statement:\nZebra Technologies leverages AI technology to evaluate job applications using objective, job-relevant criteria. This approach enhances efficiency and promotes fairness in the hiring process. However, every decision regarding interviews and hiring is made by our dedicated team, because we believe people make the best decisions about people. For more on how we use technology in hiring and how we process applicant data, see our Zebra Privacy Policy .",
