    "apply_url": "https://baxter.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/baxter/job/Bangalore-Karnataka/Apprentice_JR-213466",
    "description": "This is where your work makes a difference.\nAt Baxter, we believe every person\u2014regardless of who they are or where they are from\u2014deserves a chance to live a healthy life. It was our founding belief in 1931 and continues to be our guiding principle. We are redefining healthcare delivery to make a greater impact today, tomorrow, and beyond.\nOur Baxter colleagues are united by our Mission to Save and Sustain Lives. Together, our community is driven by a culture of courage, trust, and collaboration. Every individual is empowered to take ownership and make a meaningful impact. We strive for efficient and effective operations, and we hold each other accountable for delivering exceptional results.\nHere, you will find more than just a job\u2014you will find purpose and pride.\nYour Role at Baxter\nAt Baxter, we are committed to advancing healthcare through innovative technology solutions that improve patient outcomes. As an Apprentice , you will contribute to the design, development, testing, and support of software applications and technology solutions. You will work closely with experienced engineers to build scalable, high-quality software while gaining exposure to modern technologies, automation frameworks, and product development methodologies.\nThis role provides an excellent opportunity for early-career engineers to apply strong computer science fundamentals, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and contribute to the development of innovative healthcare solutions.\nWhat you'll be doing\n\u2022 Design, develop, test, and support software applications based on business requirements.\n\u2022 Participate in automation initiatives and integration of new technologies into existing solutions.\n\u2022 Collaborate with team members to solve technical challenges and deliver quality solutions.\n\u2022 Take ownership of assigned tasks and deliver with minimal supervision.\n\u2022 Contribute to code reviews, debugging, and continuous improvement activities.\nWhat you'll bring\n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in computer engineering, Computer Science, or Electronics & Communication Engineering.\n\u2022 Strong programming skills in Java, C, or C++.\n\u2022 Solid understanding of Object-Oriented Programming, Data Structures, Algorithms, Operating Systems, and Complexity Analysis.\n\u2022 Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.\n\u2022 Ability to work effectively in a collaborative team environment.\nEqual Employment Opportunity\nBaxter is an equal opportunity employer. Baxter evaluates qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, protected veteran status, disability/handicap status or any other legally protected characteristic.\nReasonable Accommodations\nBaxter is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities globally. If, because of a medical condition or disability, you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or interview process, please click on the link here and let us know the nature of your request along with your contact information.\nRecruitment Fraud Notice\nBaxter has discovered incidents of employment scams, where fraudulent parties pose as Baxter employees, recruiters, or other agents, and engage with online job seekers in an attempt to steal personal and/or financial information. To learn how you can protect yourself, review our Recruitment Fraud Notice .\nAI Disclaimer\nBaxter may use AI-enabled technologies to support portions of the hiring process, such as scheduling or skills matching. Final decisions regarding candidate applications and selection are made by our hiring teams, who review any AI-assisted outputs before decisions are made, and we remain committed to fairness, inclusion, and thoughtful decision-making led by our hiring teams throughout the selection process. Our AI-enabled technologies do not automatically disqualify candidates or make hiring decisions.",
