    "description": "TransUnion's Job Applicant Privacy Notice\nTeam Overview\nSales Operations Bid Management reporting into a UK manager\nThis is a hybrid position and involves regular performance of job responsibilities virtually as well as in-person at an assigned TU office location for a minimum of two days a week.\nRole Overview And Core Responsibilities\nDay To Day Responsibilities\n\u2022 Manages the end-to-end bid process from kick off to submission and post bid reviews.\n\u2022 Coordinates and develops content for high quality bid responses, ensuring compliance with client specifications and requirements.\n\u2022 Collaborates with internal teams across solutions, legal, finance, operations, HR and global technology to gather information and input for bids.\n\u2022 Writes, edits and proofreads compelling proposals, ensuring accuracy and consistency in messaging.\n\u2022 Leads bid review with senior management to ensure submissions are aligned with company objectives.\n\u2022 Monitors and tracks bid progress, setting and managing timelines to ensure deadlines are met.\n\u2022 Conducts market and competitor research to strengthen bids and understand client needs.\n\u2022 Maintains the bid library, templates and supporting documents for future use.\n\u2022 Identifies opportunities for continuous improvement in the bid process and champion to best practice.\nRequired Knowledge And Experiences\n\u2022 Degree educated an advantage, preferably in the Arts, Law or Social Sciences.\n\u2022 Strong project management skills with ability to manage multiple bids simultaneously.\n\u2022 Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and preferred experience with bid management software and CRM systems.\n\u2022 Proven track record in managing successful bids and proposals.\n\u2022 Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively across departments and levels of seniority.\n\u2022 Personal qualities include diligence, an eye for detail, strong organisational skills, deadline driven and motivated to work autonomously.\n\u2022 APMP Foundation Level Certification preferred\nTransUnion Overview:\nAt TransUnion, we encourage and are committed to creating a real, positive impact and shared sense of purpose within our Workforce for Good , which empowers our people to grow, innovate and contribute to a better future for our communities and customers. We strive to build an environment where our associates are in the driver\u2019s seat of their professional development\u2014 while having access to help along the way. We recognize that success comes when our associates thrive both professionally and personally; that\u2019s why we prioritize work/life flexibility and offer resources for our teams across the globe to collaborate and drive excellence.\nBe a part of our Workforce for Good \u2013 you\u2019ll work with great people, pioneering products and cutting-edge technology.\nTransUnion Job Title\nAnalyst, Sales Operations",
