    "id": 173,
    "normalized_key": "philips:systemsproductindustrializationengineer:pune",
    "title": "Systems Product Industrialization Engineer",
    "company": "Philips",
    "location_raw": "Pune",
    "city": "Pune",
    "job_type": "job",
    "posted_date": "2026-11-18T23:59:59+00:00",
    "apply_url": "https://philips.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/jobs-and-careers/job/Pune/Systems-Product-Industrialization-Engineer_592509",
    "description": "Job Title\nSystems Product Industrialization Engineer\nJob Description\nSystems Product Industrialization Engineer\nAs an Ultrasound Systems Product Industrialization Engineer, you will help turn new R&D designs into products that can be manufactured safely, consistently, efficiently, and at scale.\nYou will work directly with R&D, Manufacturing, Quality, Test Engineering, and suppliers to bring new Ultrasound Systems into production, implement design and process changes, and remotely help to solve technical problems encountered on the manufacturing floor.\nYour Role:\n\u2022 Partner with R&D and Manufacturing to transition new and modified Ultrasound System designs into production.\n\u2022 Evaluate new designs for manufacturability, assembly, testability, process capability, and production risk using DFM/DFA/DfX principles.\n\u2022 Develop and improve manufacturing processes, tooling, equipment, assembly methods, and production documentation.\n\u2022 Plan and execute engineering builds, manufacturing-readiness activities, process validations, Installation Qualifications, and Equipment Qualifications.\n\u2022 Create and maintain Process FMEAs, manufacturing control plans, process requirements, assembly instructions, validation documentation, and other controlled manufacturing records.\n\u2022 Create and release Manufacturing Bills of Materials, routings, and associated manufacturing master data.\n\u2022 Remotely troubleshoot technical issues on production lines and help restore production quickly when manufacturing problems result in line-down conditions.\n\u2022 Perform structured root cause analysis for design, manufacturing, process, quality, yield, and nonconforming-product issues.\n\u2022 Implement approved product and process changes across manufacturing locations and applicable supplier sites.\n\u2022 Apply Lean Manufacturing and continuous-improvement methods to reduce waste, simplify processes, improve cycle time, increase yield, and lower manufacturing cost.\n\u2022 Support engineering builds and testing needed to evaluate new products, design changes, and manufacturing processes.\n\u2022 Identify and communicate manufacturing risks to R&D and project teams, including challenging designs or schedules when product quality, manufacturability, safety, or compliance could be compromised.\n\u2022 Ensure manufacturing processes and documentation comply with applicable quality, regulatory, safety, environmental, and company requirements.\n\u2022 Support geographically distributed engineering and manufacturing teams, which will require early-morning or evening collaboration.\nYou're the Right Fit If:\n\u2022 Bachelor's Degree / Vocational Education in Mechanical Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Sciences, Cost Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Lean Manufacturing, Industrial Automation or equivalent.\n\u2022 Experience or academic exposure to manufacturing engineering, Lean Manufacturing, Process FMEA, process validation, root cause analysis, DFM/DFA/DfX, engineering change control, manufacturing documentation, or cost analysis is beneficial. For an entry-level candidate, demonstrated technical problem-solving ability and the capacity to learn are more important than having experience in every area.\nQualifications:\nWe are looking for an early-career engineer who combines solid engineering fundamentals curiosity, initiative, and a willingness to learn.\nThe successful candidate will:\n\u2022 Apply analytical thinking and engineering fundamentals to solve well-defined manufacturing problems.\n\u2022 Take ownership of assigned problems and drive them through resolution rather than waiting for step-by-step direction.\n\u2022 Know when to work independently and when an issue should be escalated or additional expertise is needed.\n\u2022 Be comfortable troubleshooting problems directly in a manufacturing environment.\n\u2022 Learn unfamiliar products, processes, and technologies quickly.\n\u2022 Produce clear, accurate, and professional engineering documentation.\n\u2022 Communicate technical issues effectively with both engineering and manufacturing audiences.\n\u2022 Work effectively across different functions, personalities, cultures, locations, and time zones.\n\u2022 Manage multiple projects and production priorities while responding appropriately to urgent manufacturing needs.\n\u2022 Maintain a strong commitment to product quality and be willing to raise concerns when schedule, cost, or other pressures could compromise quality or compliance.\n. How we work together:\nWe believe that we are better together than apart. For our office-based teams, this means working in-person at least 3 days per week.undefinedOnsite roles require full-time presence in the company\u2019s facilities.Field roles are most effectively done outside of the company\u2019s main facilities, generally at the customers\u2019 or suppliers\u2019 locations.This role is an office-based role.\nAbout Philips:\nWe are a health technology company. We built our entire company around the belief that every human matters, and we won't stop until everybody everywhere has access to the quality healthcare that we all deserve. Do the work of your life to help the lives of others.\n\u2022 Learn more about our business .\n\u2022 Discover our rich and exciting history .\n\u2022 Learn more about our purpose .\nIf you\u2019re interested in this role and have many, but not all, of the experiences needed, we encourage you to apply. You may still be the right candidate for this or other opportunities at Philips. Learn more about our culture of impact with care here .undefined\n#LI-PHILIN",
