    "apply_url": "https://lseg.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/IND-Bangalore-TowerERMZ-Infin/Associate-Content-Analyst_R0124691",
    "description": "The day-to-day responsibility would mean updating Balance Sheet, Income Statement and Cash Flow Statement, including footnote items and business, geographic and pension related segments in the database which would be key input to generate the ratio analytics and eventually flow on to the products. The data collection process would be completely governed by internal policies of LSEG. The entire updates would need to be performed within the set timelines and with expected standards of accuracy.\nMajor Responsibilities / Accountabilities:\n\u2022 Process and maintain data accurately and in a timely manner onto databases using database and financial knowledge.\n\u2022 Ensure data accuracy, timeliness and completeness are maintained as per company standards\n\u2022 Developing expertise in database and financial knowledge through continuous learning and development. Build up knowledge of financial regulations and market practices/conventions in relevant markets.\n\u2022 Maximize usage of available tools/support to best of advantage to maintain/improve content quality during daily operations.\n\u2022 Adhere to dynamic process/MoW changes, data operations standards and current data policies & procedures.\n\u2022 Responsible for delivering high productivity and quality data as per expected performance standards.\n\u2022 Proactively identify, escalate and resolve data problems.\n\u2022 Communicate & liaise with internal and external departments for resolution of data queries as per established process.\n\u2022 Test new database/application releases where appropriate, providing expert user feedback\nRequired skills and experience:\n\u2022 Should have very good understanding of accounting concepts\n\u2022 Should and be able to interpret the correlation between financial statements and know what these statements mean, what all components do they have etc.\n\u2022 Should have knowledge on IFRS GAAP, experience in Financial markets\n\u2022 Should have experience in doing deep research and should have an eye for detail\n\u2022 Technical /Professional Skills including being proficient in using outlook, excel, Teams\n\u2022 Should be a very quick learner and should display high level of agility.\n\u2022 Should have good communication skills \u2013 written and verbal.\n\u2022 Should be able to work under pressure and manage multiple tasks and flexible to work extended hours depending upon business requirements.\n\u2022 Should be flexible enough to work in different shifts at different points in time and this would include night shifts\nCareer Stage:\nAssociate\nLSEG unlocks the power of markets to create opportunities across the global economy.\nThrough our connected network of market infrastructure, data and analytics, we help customers access capital, manage risk and make confident decisions.\nOur insights bring clarity to complex markets, and our trusted services ensure resilience and stability. With deep expertise and global scale, we partner with customers to drive innovation and shape the future of finance.\nFew organisations operate at the scale, complexity and reach of LSEG. Here, you\u2019ll work alongside experts, be inspired to deliver your best work and help shape what\u2019s next for our business and the global economy.\nGuided by our values of Integrity, Partnership, Excellence and Change, we bring together diverse perspectives, encourage fresh thinking, and create an environment where learning never stops.\nJoin more than 26,000 colleagues across 60 countries, supporting customers in over 170 countries. Alongside flexible ways of working, you'll have access to benefits that support your wellbeing and your future, including 26 weeks' parental leave, healthcare, retirement planning and a wellness allowance. Through the LSEG Foundation and two paid volunteering days each year, you\u2019ll also have opportunities to get involved in your local community and support causes that matter to you.\nWe are proud to be an equal opportunities employer. This means that we do not discriminate on the basis of anyone\u2019s race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. Conforming with applicable law, we can reasonably accommodate applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs.\nPlease take a moment to read this privacy notice carefully, as it describes what personal information London Stock Exchange Group (LSEG) (we) may hold about you, what it\u2019s used for, and how it\u2019s obtained, your rights and how to contact us as a data subject .\nBy clicking on \"Apply\", the process for submitting an application will begin. If you have any questions prior to clicking \"Apply\", please contact the recruiter.\nIf you are submitting as a Recruitment Agency Partner, it is essential and your responsibility to ensure that candidates applying to LSEG are aware of this privacy notice.\nLSEG. Make more possible.",
