    "posted_date": "2026-11-16T23:59:59+00:00",
    "apply_url": "https://ag.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Airbus/job/Bangalore-Area/Intern---Maintenance-Engineering---Services_JR10449517",
    "description": "Job Description:\nJoin the Maintenance Engineering and Services team for an internship to understand how Airbus maximizes operational availability for airlines worldwide.\nYou will shadow our Maintenance Program & Services Engineers, observe the lifecycle of Scheduled Maintenance Services and gain foundational exposure to core industry concepts of Aircraft Maintenance Planning and regulations.\nThis program will help you learn about but not limited to\n\u2022 Airbus fleet optimization strategies\n\u2022 Contribute to Direct Maintenance Costs reductions.\n\u2022 Establish and deliver timely and consistent solutions to the requests raised by the customers.\n\u2022 Managing the production of Scheduled Maintenance Services, covering all Airbus A/C program\n\u2022 Ensuring that airlines maintenance programmes/planning deliverables are performed in accordance with customer's expectations\n\u2022 Contributing Technical Data improvement/transformation project as Technical Data Aircraft System - Business Operations representative.\nRequirements:\nAs the successful candidate, you will have to demonstrate the following competencies:\nYou will have the following skills and experience:\n\u2022 Educated to an AME / degree level (or equivalent) in Engineering or a related discipline,\n\u2022 General technical knowledge of aircraft, their maintenance & their operations\n\u2022 Well organized and structured with good computer knowledge / GSuite\n\u2022 Knowledge of EASA Part-M regulation, Airlines/MRO (Maintenance Repair and Overhaul) - Part M /145\n\u2022 Strong communication and presentation skills\n\u2022 Highly Customer service oriented\nIn addition, the successful candidate will be able to demonstrate the following skills:\n\u2022 Good listener, proactive and creative\n\u2022 Reactivity and adaptability in a changing and demanding environment\n\u2022 Negotiation level of English, another language would be a plus.\nThis job requires an awareness of any potential compliance risks and a commitment to act with integrity, as the foundation for the Company\u2019s success, reputation and sustainable growth.\nCompany:\nAirbus India Private Limited\nEmployment Type:\nInternship -------\nExperience Level:\nStudent\nJob Family:\nCustomer Eng.&Technical Support&Services\nBy submitting your CV or application you are consenting to Airbus using and storing information about you for monitoring purposes relating to your application or future employment. This information will only be used by Airbus.\nAirbus is committed to achieving workforce diversity and creating an inclusive working environment. We welcome all applications irrespective of social and cultural background, age, gender, disability, sexual orientation or religious belief.\nAirbus is, and always has been, committed to equal opportunities for all. As such, we will never ask for any type of monetary exchange in the frame of a recruitment process. Any impersonation of Airbus to do so should be reported to emsom@airbus.com .\nAt Airbus, we support you to work, connect and collaborate more easily and flexibly. Wherever possible, we foster flexible working arrangements to stimulate innovative thinking.",
