    "apply_url": "https://lseg.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/IND-Bangalore-A-RMZ-Infinity/Associate-Content-Analyst---German-Language-Specialist_R0122646",
    "description": "Associate Content Analyst \u2013 Deals & Private Equity, Bangalore\nThe Associate Content Analyst role is within Deals Content team responsible for collection, maintenance, analysis and dissemination of high-quality information. Based on data that you will collect and analyze, Refinitiv issues League Tables where we present top financial and legal advisors, who worked on transactions all over the world. You will play a crucial role in collecting the data, cooperating with contributors to League Tables and internal stakeholders, answering their questions and explaining content and structure of League Tables and single transactions. Based on data that you search, analyse and send to our products, thousands\nof M&A professionals around the world will be able to benchmark their performance against market and that will help them to make strategic decisions regarding their business.\nThe position is offered on local terms and will require working in shifts. The position will report to the Team Leader, Deals.\nWHAT DO YOU NEED TO BRING?\nFluent in English and communicative (reading) in German language\nAbility to work both independently and as part of a team\nGreat attention to details\nSelf-motivated even when attending to routine tasks\nAbility to prioritize tasks and work effectively under time pressure\nProfessional attitude\nCuriosity in global economic trends\nYOU WILL BE EVEN MORE COMPETITIVE IF:\nGeneral interest in new internet technologies and trends would represent an advantage\nTechnical skills and basic knowledge of VBA, SQL or advanced excel will be a strong plus\nGraduate preferably in Business, Finance or Economics related fields\nSOME OF DAILY TASKS YOU WILL PERFORM:\nProvide clients with data related to Deals events (mergers and acquisitions, public equity offerings and private equity)\nResearch and collect relevant data in line with the methodology\nEnsure the data is provided in a timely and accurate manner\nCollaborate with other teams within Refinitiv\nInteract with clients who work on data we provide, listen to their feedback and implement automation and quality improvement solutions to address their concerns\nWe maximize each employee\u2019s potential through personal development and through a wide range of learning tools both formal and informal. We believe that remunerating our people with competitive salaries and a range of attractive benefits such as:\nYou will be provided with full training and assistance of your colleagues.\nCareer Stage:\nAssociate\nLSEG unlocks the power of markets to create opportunities across the global economy.\nThrough our connected network of market infrastructure, data and analytics, we help customers access capital, manage risk and make confident decisions.\nOur insights bring clarity to complex markets, and our trusted services ensure resilience and stability. With deep expertise and global scale, we partner with customers to drive innovation and shape the future of finance.\nFew organisations operate at the scale, complexity and reach of LSEG. Here, you\u2019ll work alongside experts, be inspired to deliver your best work and help shape what\u2019s next for our business and the global economy.\nGuided by our values of Integrity, Partnership, Excellence and Change, we bring together diverse perspectives, encourage fresh thinking, and create an environment where learning never stops.\nJoin more than 26,000 colleagues across 60 countries, supporting customers in over 170 countries. Alongside flexible ways of working, you'll have access to benefits that support your wellbeing and your future, including 26 weeks' parental leave, healthcare, retirement planning and a wellness allowance. Through the LSEG Foundation and two paid volunteering days each year, you\u2019ll also have opportunities to get involved in your local community and support causes that matter to you.\nWe are proud to be an equal opportunities employer. This means that we do not discriminate on the basis of anyone\u2019s race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. Conforming with applicable law, we can reasonably accommodate applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs.\nPlease take a moment to read this privacy notice carefully, as it describes what personal information London Stock Exchange Group (LSEG) (we) may hold about you, what it\u2019s used for, and how it\u2019s obtained, your rights and how to contact us as a data subject .\nBy clicking on \"Apply\", the process for submitting an application will begin. If you have any questions prior to clicking \"Apply\", please contact the recruiter.\nIf you are submitting as a Recruitment Agency Partner, it is essential and your responsibility to ensure that candidates applying to LSEG are aware of this privacy notice.\nLSEG. Make more possible.",
