    "description": "Job Description\nWhat will you work on?\n\u2022 Social Media Management: Assist in managing Dineout Mag\u2019s social media pages and maintaining a consistent posting schedule\n\u2022 Content Calendar & Scheduling: Help plan, organise, schedule, and publish content across platforms.\n\u2022 Content Strategy & Execution: Support the execution of social media strategies and content series to improve reach and engagement.\n\u2022 Page Management: Keep pages updated by managing stories, bios, highlights, comments, DMs, and broadcast channels.\n\u2022 Audience Engagement: Create interactive stories, engage with followers, and help build an active online community.\n\u2022 Performance Tracking: Monitor content performance, track key metrics, and share insights to help improve engagement and reach.\n\u2022 Trendspotting: Stay updated on social media trends, formats, and relevant F&B conversations to identify content opportunities.\n\u2022 LinkedIn Support: Assist in creating and publishing content that strengthens Dineout Mag\u2019s professional presence.\n\u2022 Creator Collaborations: Identify potential creators and influencers for collaborations and audience growth.\nWho are we looking for?\n\u2022 3-6 months of experience in social media management or a related role; relevant internship experience is welcome.\n\u2022 Hands-on familiarity with Instagram and other social media platforms.\n\u2022 Strong written and verbal communication skills, with an eye for detail.\n\u2022 A good understanding of social media trends, content formats, and audience engagement.\n\u2022 Basic knowledge of social media analytics and performance metrics.\n\u2022 An interest in food, restaurants, and the F&B landscape is a plus.\n\u2022 A proactive, organised, and creative individual who can work well in a fast-paced environment.\nWe are an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law.\n\nAdditional Information\nVisit our tech blogs to learn more about some the challenges we deal with: https://medium.com/swiggy-bytes\nWe are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by the law.",
