    "description": "Position Summary\nThe selected candidate for this role will be responsible for a range of activities supporting Finance Services Operations activities daily as directed by senior colleagues in the team.\nRole Responsibilities\n\u2022 Processes financial transactions on a daily basis, ensuring that accounting processes and controls are adhered\n\u2022 Processes and files correspondence and ensure that appropriate records are accurately maintained\n\u2022 Manages the status of accounts and balances and identifies inconsistencies\n\u2022 Supports the process for monthly, quarterly and year-end financial reporting as required\n\u2022 Ensures adherence to reporting and regulatory requirements\n\u2022 Ensures processes are followed in a timely manner and in line with agreed terms\n\u2022 Support wider the finance teams where volumes are high/resolution complex to ensure group KPI targets and management reporting deadlines are met.\n\u2022 Ad hoc reporting and requests from Group and/or local finance as required.\nPreferred Skills and Experience\n\u2022 Entry level Finance degree/professional qualification from a reputed institute.\n\u2022 Good knowledge on accounting concepts and principles.\n\u2022 Good Knowledge of Microsoft Office Packages.\n\u2022 Excellent oral and written English communication\n\u2022 Responsible attitude and sense of teamwork\n\u2022 Detail focus, and accuracy orientation.\n\u2022 Ability to work according to UK work hours.\n\u2022 Planning and prioritising according to business needs.\nAt LSEG we embrace diversity and actively seek to attract individuals with unique backgrounds and perspectives. We break down barriers and encourage collaboration, enabling innovation and rapid development of solutions that make a difference. Our workplace generates an enriching and rewarding experience for our people and customers alike. Our vision is to build an inclusive culture in which everyone feels driven to reach their potential.\nWe know that real personal growth cannot be achieved by simply climbing a career ladder \u2013 which is why we encourage and enable a wealth of avenues and interesting opportunities for everyone to broaden and deepen their skills and expertise.\nLSEG are committed to supporting emotional, physical, financial and societal wellbeing. Our tailored benefits are a key part of this commitment and we offer colleagues a range of support from healthcare and retirement planning to paid volunteering days and consumer discounts.\nWe also make reasonable accommodations for applicants and employees with disabilities. If an accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other benefits and privileges of employment, please make your recruiter aware, we want to ensure you perform at your best.\nAs a global organisation spanning 70 countries and one rooted in a culture of growth, opportunity, diversity and innovation, LSEG is a place where everyone can grow, develop and fulfil your potential with purposeful careers.\nPlease take a moment to read this privacy notice carefully, as it describes what personal information the London Stock Exchange Group (LSEG) (\u201cWe\u201d) may hold about you, what it\u2019s used for, and how it\u2019s obtained, your rights and how to contact us as a data subject.\nIf you are submitting as a Recruitment Agency Partner, it is essential and your responsibility to ensure that candidates applying to LSEG are aware of this privacy notice.\nCareer Stage:\nAssociate\nLSEG unlocks the power of markets to create opportunities across the global economy.\nThrough our connected network of market infrastructure, data and analytics, we help customers access capital, manage risk and make confident decisions.\nOur insights bring clarity to complex markets, and our trusted services ensure resilience and stability. With deep expertise and global scale, we partner with customers to drive innovation and shape the future of finance.\nFew organisations operate at the scale, complexity and reach of LSEG. Here, you\u2019ll work alongside experts, be inspired to deliver your best work and help shape what\u2019s next for our business and the global economy.\nGuided by our values of Integrity, Partnership, Excellence and Change, we bring together diverse perspectives, encourage fresh thinking, and create an environment where learning never stops.\nJoin more than 26,000 colleagues across 60 countries, supporting customers in over 170 countries. Alongside flexible ways of working, you'll have access to benefits that support your wellbeing and your future, including 26 weeks' parental leave, healthcare, retirement planning and a wellness allowance. Through the LSEG Foundation and two paid volunteering days each year, you\u2019ll also have opportunities to get involved in your local community and support causes that matter to you.\nWe are proud to be an equal opportunities employer. This means that we do not discriminate on the basis of anyone\u2019s race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. Conforming with applicable law, we can reasonably accommodate applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs.\nPlease take a moment to read this privacy notice carefully, as it describes what personal information London Stock Exchange Group (LSEG) (we) may hold about you, what it\u2019s used for, and how it\u2019s obtained, your rights and how to contact us as a data subject .\nBy clicking on \"Apply\", the process for submitting an application will begin. If you have any questions prior to clicking \"Apply\", please contact the recruiter.\nIf you are submitting as a Recruitment Agency Partner, it is essential and your responsibility to ensure that candidates applying to LSEG are aware of this privacy notice.\nLSEG. Make more possible.",
