    "description": "Job Location\nMUMBAI GENERAL OFFICE\nJob Description\nFinance & Accounting at P&G plays a key role in business strategy, decision-making, planning and performance management .\nAs a CA Intern , you will join P&G for a 1-year internship and work on meaningful Finance assignments across brands, businesses, functions or key projects. From Day 1, you will take ownership of defined responsibilities, work with Finance leaders and cross-functional teams, and use financial analysis and business insights to support decision-making.\nThe internship provides practical exposure to Finance in a leading FMCG organization while building your financial, analytical, business partnering and leadership capabilities .\nKey Responsibilities\n\u2022 Support financial analysis, planning, forecasting and performance management .\n\u2022 Analyze financial and business data to identify trends, risks, opportunities and actionable insights .\n\u2022 Partner with Finance and cross-functional teams to support business and strategic decisions .\n\u2022 Take ownership of assigned Finance projects and deliverables .\n\u2022 Gain exposure to areas such as Commercial Finance, Accounting, Internal Controls, Tax and Treasury , depending on the assignment.\n\u2022 Support improvements in financial processes, reporting and controls.\n\u2022 Communicate financial insights clearly to relevant stakeholders.\n\u2022 Demonstrate ownership, integrity and sound financial stewardship .\nJob Qualifications\n\u2022 CA Intermediate qualified in the first attempt.\n\u2022 Eligible to undertake the 1-year CA internship/articleship as per applicable ICAI requirements.\n\u2022 Strong academic record.\n\u2022 Strong analytical, financial and problem-solving skills .\n\u2022 Good written and verbal English communication skills.\n\u2022 Strong interpersonal and collaboration skills.\n\u2022 Ability to manage multiple priorities and take ownership of deliverables.\n\u2022 Strong interest in Finance, business and decision-making .\n\u2022 Demonstrated initiative, learning agility and willingness to take on challenging assignments.\nWhat We Offer\n\u2022 Meaningful Finance responsibilities from Day 1.\n\u2022 Exposure to real business and financial decision-making.\n\u2022 Continuous coaching and mentoring from experienced Finance professionals.\n\u2022 Opportunities to work with Finance and cross-functional teams.\n\u2022 On-the-job learning to develop technical Finance, analytical, business partnering and leadership skills .\nJob Schedule\nFull time\nJob Number\nR000162371\nJob Segmentation\nInternships",
