    "description": "About Workato\nWorkato is the leading Control and Execution Platform for Enterprise AI \u2014 the neutral platform enterprises trust to put AI to work across their business. Workato unifies data, applications, and processes into a single platform so AI can reliably orchestrate business processes in production at enterprise scale. Built on more than a decade of running mission-critical processes for over half the Fortune 500 \u2014 including Nasdaq, Amazon, Cisco, Vodafone, Atlassian, and Lucid Motors \u2014 Workato turns over 14,000 enterprise systems AI needs to act on into one governed execution layer. For more information, visit workato.com .\nWhy join us?\nUltimately, Workato believes in fostering a flexible, trust-oriented culture that empowers everyone to take full ownership of their roles . We are driven by innovation and looking for team players who want to actively build our company.\nBut, we also believe in balancing productivity with self-care . That\u2019s why we offer all of our employees a vibrant and dynamic work environment along with a multitude of benefits they can enjoy inside and outside of their work lives.\nIf this sounds right up your alley, please submit an application. We look forward to getting to know you!\nAlso, feel free to check out why:\n\u2022\nBusiness Insider named us an \u201centerprise startup to bet your career on\u201d\n\u2022\nForbes\u2019 Cloud 100 recognized us as one of the top 100 private cloud companies in the world\n\u2022\nDeloitte Tech Fast 500 ranked us as the 17th fastest growing tech company in the Bay Area, and 96th in North America\n\u2022\nQuartz ranked us the #1 best company for remote workers\nResponsibilities\nWe are looking for an exceptional Automation Engineer Intern to join our team. In this role, you will support the SaaS applications and platforms that power our demo and field environments, investigating access issues, misconfigurations, and recurring requests. You will focus on identifying root causes, developing lasting solutions, and documenting your findings. Working alongside Automation Engineers and Field Systems Analysts, you will receive regular mentorship, take ownership of well-scoped problems, and identify opportunities to automate repetitive work using Workato.\nIn this role, you will also be responsible for:\n\u2022\nAssist with acquiring and setting up SaaS, PaaS, and IaaS platforms for demos and proofs of concept, including Salesforce, SAP, Workday, NetSuite, ServiceNow, Snowflake, AWS, and GCP, ensuring environments meet user requirements.\n\u2022\nCollaborate with technical teams to keep demo applications integrated and functioning as expected.\n\u2022\nAdminister demo applications by adding users, configuring permissions, and assigning licenses.\n\u2022\nSupport complex application configurations and verify that they align with organizational requirements.\n\u2022\nReview application settings regularly to help maintain performance and security.\n\u2022\nSupport users in accessing demo environments and applications, serving as the first point of contact for their requests.\n\u2022\nInvestigate and troubleshoot access problems, misconfigurations, and failed logins, identifying root causes and recommending lasting solutions.\n\u2022\nAssist with routine governance activities, including access reviews, license tracking, and compliance checks, and flag any anomalies.\n\u2022\nIdentify recurring issues and repetitive manual tasks, and propose or help build automations and tools on Workato to manage demo infrastructure.\n\u2022\nHelp build and maintain environments that support high-quality Workato product demonstrations.\n\u2022\nDocument troubleshooting steps, configurations, and how-to guides to make solutions repeatable.\n\u2022\nKeep stakeholders informed of request status and escalate blockers promptly.\n\u2022\nShare findings and lessons learned with the team, including approaches tried and their outcomes.\nRequirements\nQualifications / Experience / Technical Skills\n\u2022\nDegree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.\n\u2022\nDemonstrated problem-solving ability through coursework, projects, work, or personal experience involving the diagnosis and resolution of a complex issue.\n\u2022\nHands-on exposure to at least one SaaS application or administration console, such as Google Workspace, Slack, Salesforce, Okta, or Jira.\n\u2022\nBasic understanding of user access concepts, including roles, permissions, and least privilege.\n\u2022\nProfessional working proficiency in English.\n\u2022\nExperience delivering a project involving application, integration, or system troubleshooting is a plus.\n\u2022\nExposure to cloud platforms such as AWS or GCP, or enterprise applications such as Salesforce, Workday, or NetSuite, is a plus.\n\u2022\nFamiliarity with single sign-on and identity concepts, including SAML, OAuth, and MFA, is a plus.\n\u2022\nBasic scripting or low-code/no-code automation experience using Workato, Python, or similar tools is a plus.\n\u2022\nExperience using spreadsheets or data tools for analysis and reporting is a plus.\n\u2022\nInterest in IT governance, security, or compliance is a plus.\nSoft Skills / Personal Characteristics\n\u2022\nMethodical approach to problem-solving, with a focus on understanding issues and identifying root causes before proposing solutions.\n\u2022\nStrong analytical mindset, with the ability to gather information from multiple sources, question assumptions, and draw evidence-based conclusions.\n\u2022\nPersistence when facing blockers, with sound judgment about when to escalate or ask for help.\n\u2022\nClear written communication skills, with the ability to explain problems, reasoning, and solutions so others can follow.\n\u2022\nStrong attention to detail and a consistent habit of verifying work.\n(REQ ID: 3000)",
