    "description": "APM Terminals\nPosition Title: Inland Associate -Documentation\nWorking Location:\nMaersk CFS, Ground Floor No 78, Anuppam pattu village, Minjur, Ponneri Taluka, Thiruvalluvar dist,\nChennai- 601203 India\nJob Description:\nInland Associate CFS Import documentation:\n\u2022 Responsible for CFS -import documentation & billing.\n\u2022 Follow up on CFS documentation process & compliance in line with SOP.\n\u2022 Ensure to collect appropriate documents from customers viz BL/BOE/OOC/DO etc. during gate IN & OUT of cargo/container from CFS.\n\u2022 Uploading IAL in system/work order/gate-out pass generation & billing.\n\u2022 Endorsing container/cargo availability status in CFS to customs after thorough check in system.\n\u2022 Accountable for documenting customs detained cargo/container and submitting report to customs as and when required.\n\u2022 Billing to customers using CFS tariff and contract rate.\n\u2022 Ensure timely billing to customers with error free service.\n\u2022 Ensure on payment collection with cashier on invoicing for cash customer.\n\u2022 Interacting with shipping lines in case of the contingency regarding DO/BL.\n\u2022 Reconciliation with empty container post de-stuffing on daily basis.\n\u2022 Ensure to validate manual billing & receipt of payment while issuing manual gate out pass.\n\u2022 Invoice follow up with vendor and process it for on time payment.\n\u2022 Responsible for preparing and sending timely MIS/ periodic reports to the respective stake holders.\n\u2022 Working in co-ordination with customs officials, customer service & cashier team on day-to-day activities.\n\u2022 Interaction with control tower team in case of contingency on laden container arrival & empty container evacuation.\n\u2022 Ability to understand customers (CHA-Importer-consignee) needs and helping them out in pleasant manner.\n\u2022 Support customer service in customer query resolution.\n\u2022 Timely responding to e-mail queries to the customers, related to documentation/invoicing.\n\u2022 Pre-planning and communicating internal team on special request from customer.\n\u2022 Understanding characteristics of hazardous cargo and HSSE compliance.\nWhat we are looking for:\n\u2022 Basic knowledge in CFS related activities-Export/import/bonding/warehousing.\n\u2022 Fundamental knowledge in systems.\n\u2022 Analytical skills\n\u2022 Problem solving\n\u2022 Multitasking ability\nMaersk is committed to a diverse and inclusive workplace, and we embrace different styles of thinking. Maersk is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applicants without regard to race, colour, gender, sex, age, religion, creed, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, sexual orientation, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy or parental leave, veteran status, gender identity, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We will consider qualified applicants with criminal histories in a manner consistent with all legal requirements.\nWe are happy to support your need for any adjustments during the application and hiring process. If you need special assistance or an accommodation to use our website, apply for a position, or to perform a job, please contact us by emailing accommodationrequests@maersk.com .",
