    "description": "Job Description:\nJob Title: Operations Analyst\nCorporate Title: Analyst\nLocation: Jaipur, India\nRole Description\n\u2022 The person will be responsible for day-to-day review of voice logs between Client Relationship Managers (RC) and clients where trade details are discussed and agreed. They need to ensure that all key trade-related details are clearly discussed, accurately captured, and documented in the applicable product-specific template. The role requires strong attention to detail, adherence to defined review standards, timely completion of assigned production duties, and appropriate escalation of exceptions, missing information, or first-level queries within the pre-specified timelines. The candidate should also act as a backup for peers when required and share best practices with the team to support consistent quality delivery.\nWhat we\u2019ll offer you\nAs part of our flexible scheme, here are just some of the benefits that you\u2019ll enjoy,\n\u2022 Best in class leave policy.\n\u2022 Gender neutral parental leaves\n\u2022 100% reimbursement under childcare assistance benefit (gender neutral)\n\u2022 Sponsorship for Industry relevant certifications and education\n\u2022 Employee Assistance Program for you and your family members\n\u2022 Comprehensive Hospitalization Insurance for you and your dependents\n\u2022 Accident and Term life Insurance\n\u2022 Complementary Health screening for 35 yrs. and above\nYour key responsibilities\n\u2022 Review voice logs between RCs and clients to validate that trade details have been discussed and agreed as per the required standards.\n\u2022 Listen to and understand client and RMs discussions and accurately document the agreed details or the prescribed business template, as applicable.\n\u2022 Complete the relevant product-specific voice log review template with accurate details, observations, and outcome of the review.\n\u2022 Identify and highlight missing, incomplete, inconsistent, or unclear trade details and escalate exceptions to the relevant stakeholders within agreed timelines.\n\u2022 Ensure accurate and timely completion of daily production activities in line with defined SLAs, cut-off times, and quality expectations.\n\u2022 Perform quality checks on completed reviews to support consistency, audit readiness, and control effectiveness.\n\u2022 Assist in preparing and reviewing daily control / production reports, including tracking of open items, exceptions, and follow-ups.\n\u2022 Support follow-up with RC / business teams for clarification or resolution of deficiencies noted during voice log review.\n\u2022 Maintain proper documentation and evidence of review outcomes to support internal control, audit, and management reporting requirements.\n\u2022 Coordinate with team members and stakeholders on complex cases, escalations, reporting requirements, and process improvements.\n\u2022 Act as backup for peers during absence and support knowledge sharing, cross-training, and continuous improvement within the team.\n\u2022 Perform other administration, reporting, and control-related tasks as assigned.\nYour skills and experience\n\u2022 Minimum educational qualification: University graduate with a Bachelor\u2019s Degree.\n\u2022 Good command of business English for accurate documentation, exception reporting, and stakeholder communication.\n\u2022 Understanding of trade lifecycle, banking / wealth management products, or control review processes will be an added advantage.\n\u2022 Strong listening, comprehension, documentation, and analytical skills with high attention to detail.\n\u2022 Ability to identify gaps, inconsistencies, missing information, and potential control issues from recorded conversations.\n\u2022 Candidates are required to be proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Excel, Word, and PowerPoint.\n\u2022 Highly motivated, quality-focused, and able to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team environment.\n\u2022 Ability to multi-task and work under pressure to meet production timelines, cut-off times, and quality standards.\n\u2022 Good communication skills and ability to manage routine queries / first-level escalations professionally.\nProven ability to leverage AI tools to enhance productivity, optimise workflows to solve business problems, while applying critical judgment to ensure responsible and ethical use of data and AI outputs.\nHow we\u2019ll support you\n\u2022 Training and development to help you excel in your career.\n\u2022 Coaching and support from experts in your team.\n\u2022 A culture of continuous learning to aid progression.\n\u2022 A range of flexible benefits that you can tailor to suit your needs.\nAbout us and our teams\nPlease visit our company website for further information:\nhttps://www.db.com/company/company.html\nWe strive for a culture in which we are empowered to excel together every day. This includes acting responsibly, thinking commercially, taking initiative and working collaboratively.\nTogether we share and celebrate the successes of our people. Together we are Deutsche Bank Group.\nWe welcome applications from all people and promote a positive, fair and inclusive work environment.",
