    "apply_url": "https://www.rubrik.com/company/careers/departments/job.8345283?gh_jid=8345283",
    "description": "Product Management Intern \u2013 Identity Resilience\nAbout the Team & Role\nThe Product Management team at Rubrik drives forward our vision of delivering a market-leading platform that addresses the world\u2019s most critical cyber resilience and data security challenges.\nThe Identity Resilience team is Rubrik\u2019s fastest-growing business unit, operating with a high-velocity \"0-to-1\" charter. Today, modern cyberattacks almost exclusively weaponize identity systems. When identity fails, the entire enterprise halts. Our mission is to ensure enterprise identity environments are secure, observable, compliant, and instantly recoverable.\nWe are looking for a strategically sharp, technical, and execution-minded Product Management Intern for a high-impact 2-month internship based in Bengaluru. As an intern, you will own a core strategic initiative \u2013 bridging enterprise customer pain points, competitive differentiation, and technical architecture to deliver a concrete product roadmap for next-generation identity protection.\nWhat You\u2019ll Do (2-Month Charter)\n\u2022 Market Landscape & Threat Vector Analysis: Benchmark the enterprise identity attack surface across hybrid environments. Map emerging threat vectors to potential resilience and recovery capabilities.\n\u2022 Customer Discovery & Pain Point Synthesis: Work alongside PM and GTM mentors to analyze customer requirements, telemetry data, and enterprise security frameworks to pinpoint the highest-friction operational gaps for Security and IAM teams.\n\u2022 Feature Strategy & PRD Ownership: Define the scope, user workflows, and success metrics for a targeted identity protection/recovery feature. Author a high-quality Product Requirement Document (PRD) balancing enterprise-grade depth with Rubrik\u2019s trademark simplicity.\n\u2022 Cross-Functional Architecture Alignment: Collaborate closely with Engineering, UX Design, and Architecture leads to evaluate technical trade-offs, define API/data pipeline requirements, and ensure feasibility.\n\u2022 Executive Strategy Pitch: Conclude your internship with an Executive Product Readout to Senior Leadership, defending your business case, technical trade-offs, and proposed roadmap.\nWhat You\u2019ll Need\n\u2022 Education: Currently enrolled in a premier MBA/management program (IIM, ISB, or equivalent global top-tier business school) graduating in 2027/28\n\u2022 Technical Foundation: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or an equivalent engineering discipline. Prior product management or technical experience in enterprise systems, cloud platforms, or cybersecurity is a strong plus.\n\u2022 Systems & Security Thinking: An understanding of enterprise software fundamentals; familiarity with core identity concepts is an advantage.\n\u2022 Problem Solving: Comfort with ambiguity, structured thinking, and the ability to break complex, undefined problems into crisp, actionable requirements.\n\u2022 Communication & Influence: Exceptional written and verbal communication skills with the ability to articulate technical trade-offs to senior product and engineering leaders.\n\u2022 Location: Based in or willing to relocate to Bengaluru for the 2-month internship duration (Hybrid model).\nWhat You\u2019ll Gain\n\u2022 True 0-to-1 Problem Ownership: Direct ownership of a real-world, high-priority product problem in enterprise cybersecurity \u2013 not a back-burner sandbox project.\n\u2022 High-Stakes Leadership Visibility: Regular 1:1 mentorship from seasoned Product Managers and a final presentation to Product & Engineering leadership.\n\u2022 Cybersecurity PM Expertise: Hands-on exposure to cutting-edge identity governance, threat modeling, and resilience frameworks inside an enterprise security market leader.\nJoin Us in Securing and Accelerating the World's AI Transformation\nRubrik (NYSE: RBRK) is the Security and AI Operations Company, delivering one platform built at the intersection of data, identity, and AI. The platform enables agentic cyber resilience and trusted AI operations for enterprises worldwide, built to recover before disruption strikes and stay a step ahead, so security is never the reason ambition stalls.\nLinkedin | X (formerly Twitter) | Instagram | Rubrik.com\nInclusion @ Rubrik\nAt Rubrik, we are dedicated to fostering a culture where people from all backgrounds are valued, feel they belong, and believe they can succeed. Our commitment to inclusion is at the heart of our mission to secure the world\u2019s data.\nOur goal is to hire and promote the best talent, regardless of background. We continually review our hiring practices to ensure fairness and strive to create an environment where every employee has equal access to opportunities for growth and excellence. We believe in empowering everyone to bring their authentic selves to work and achieve their fullest potential.\nOur inclusion strategy focuses on three core areas of our business and culture:\n\u2022\nOur Company: We are committed to building a merit-based organization that offers equal access to growth and success for all employees globally. Your potential is limitless here.\n\u2022\nOur Culture: We strive to create an inclusive atmosphere where individuals from all backgrounds feel a strong sense of belonging, can thrive, and do their best work. Your contributions help us innovate and break boundaries.\n\u2022\nOur Communities: We are dedicated to expanding our engagement with the communities we operate in, creating opportunities for underrepresented talent and driving greater innovation for our clients. Your impact extends beyond Rubrik, contributing to safer and stronger communities.\nEqual Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled\nRubrik is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Rubrik provides equal employment opportunities to employees and applicants in all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, training, leave, and termination.\nRubrik provides reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities in accordance with applicable law. If you need an accommodation to participate in the application process or to perform your job, please contact hr@rubrik.com . Accommodations may include changes to the application process, documents in an alternate format, a sign language interpreter, or specialized equipment.\nEEO IS THE LAW\nNOTIFICATION OF EMPLOYEE RIGHTS UNDER FEDERAL LABOR LAWS",
