    "apply_url": "https://ag.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Airbus/job/Bangalore-Area/FTM-Intern_JR10448390",
    "description": "Job Description:\nInternship Job Description\nDuration : 6 months\nJob title : FTM Intern.\nYour main missions will consist of :\nA) Accountabilities \u25cf The Jobholder is responsible for the deliverables and accountabilities as defined under main activities by the respective trade / department domain heads.\nB) Dimensions \u25cf There is no team or budget responsibility linked to this position.\nC) Main activities\n\u25cf Data collection and analysis of the delays and defects\n\u25cf Reviewing the Technical publications such as AD, SB and VSBs\n\u25cf Coordinating with various FTM (CAMO) divisions for smooth induction / acceptance of the major assemblies such as landing gear, Engines etc.\n\u25cf Basic data review / collection from component shop reports (SFR) & other miscellaneous project\n\u25cf Defining and maintaining customer aircraft configuration data in ERP / MIS\n\u25cf Supporting the ARC and CMR related documents preparation and standardization of the associated processes\n\u25cf Updation of structural damage/repair data in the required reporting templates\n\u25cf WGR management & data sanity checks.\n\u25cf Managing Engineering Statistical Report (ESR)\n\u25cf Creating and managing RCP reports for all FTM contracts\n\u25cf Review and preparation of the AMP / OMP\n\u25cf Supporting trade engineers on day to day engineering functions 2.Technical Records Based at FHS-TSP Central site, FHS-TSP Technical Recorder Intern will associate in managing the following activities :\n\u25cf Review for completeness of all maintenance and operational documentation (including maintenance checks, work orders, Technical LogBook\u2026).\n\u25cf Continuously input data into AFHS Maintenance Information System (MIS).\n\u25cf Ensuring that the records are maintained and updated to the highest quality standard in both documentation and in the Maintenance Information System (MIS) with regards to Continuing Airworthiness Management. Internship Job Description\n\u25cf Provides Technical support for Aircrafts Induction/Leasing/Re-delivery and Airworthiness Review.\n\u25cf Compilation / amendment of aircraft configuration control documents:\n\u25cf AD/SB/EO Compliance file.\n\u25cf Back to birth file for Engine, APU, Propeller, Landing gear LLP\u2019s.\n\u25cf Aircraft Inspection Report components file, HTC file, Structure file\n\u25cf Original documents folder (Delivery doc\u2019s).Maintenance summary status reports, Last done next due (LDND) tasks as per approved AMP.\n\u25cf Contribute to Kardex configuration update activity.\n\u25cf Address quality finding on Technical records and launch necessary actions towards the various actors (MRO, MOC-MCC, Technical Services\u2026) to align documentation and MIS content.\n\u25cf Actively reports safety related issues and any other FTM related issues, and in relation, participates in the whole process of finding a resolution to avoid future reoccurrence.\n\u25cf Guaranteeing an excellent level of service with the local teams in charge of the interface with the customer. 3.Maintenance Planning Based at FHS-TSP Central site, FHS-TSP Maintenance Planner intern will associate in managing the following activities:\n\u25cf Remotely overseas customer\u2019s A/C fleet maintenance planning on several bases\n\u25cf Closely coordinates with TSP Local team to ensure efficient planning and on time performance of maintenance in Line Maintenance or Base Maintenance. \u25cf Ensures that the maintenance activities are in compliance with the customer's approved maintenance program.\n\u25cf Processes customer work requirements.\n\u25cf Manages Long Term Planning and Base Maintenance Work Packages\n\u25cf Maximizes effective maintenance task interval accomplishment, while ensuring compliance with customer and airworthiness requirements.\n\u25cf Prepares and generates Maintenance Planning related reports and status.\n\u25cf Monitors maintenance status and modifications in work to ensure all targets are met.\n\u25cf Safeguards the airworthiness and safety of the customer's fleet through strictly controlled and well-scheduled maintenance events to keep the aircraft in the highest industry standard.\n\u25cf Develops effective and efficient maintenance packages with appropriate control and progress planning to ensure smooth on time compliance of maintenance tasks.\n\u25cf Guarantees that the Maintenance Information System meets a quality standard necessary to ensure Airworthiness of the fleet.\n\u25cf Actively reports safety related issues and any other FTM related issues, and in relation, participates in the whole process of finding a resolution to avoid future recurrence.\n\u25cf Guaranteeing an excellent level of service with the local teams in charge of the interface with the customer. E. Job Requirement\nYou possess the following competences:\n\u25cf Basic knowledge of PART M and PART 145.\n\u25cf Basic Computer knowledge\n\u25cf Excellent team player with good communication and interpersonal skills\nQualifications: Minimum degree holder in Aerospace/Mechanical Engineering or AME BAMEEC (Basic Aircraft Maintenance Engineer's Examination certificate) Holder in B1/B2 Stream.\nThis job requires an awareness of any potential compliance risks and a commitment to act with integrity, as the foundation for the Company\u2019s success, reputation and sustainable growth.\nCompany:\nAirbus India Private Limited\nEmployment Type:\nInternship -------\nExperience Level:\nStudent\nJob Family:\nCustomer Eng.&Technical Support&Services\nBy submitting your CV or application you are consenting to Airbus using and storing information about you for monitoring purposes relating to your application or future employment. This information will only be used by Airbus.\nAirbus is committed to achieving workforce diversity and creating an inclusive working environment. We welcome all applications irrespective of social and cultural background, age, gender, disability, sexual orientation or religious belief.\nAirbus is, and always has been, committed to equal opportunities for all. As such, we will never ask for any type of monetary exchange in the frame of a recruitment process. Any impersonation of Airbus to do so should be reported to emsom@airbus.com .\nAt Airbus, we support you to work, connect and collaborate more easily and flexibly. Wherever possible, we foster flexible working arrangements to stimulate innovative thinking.",
