    "description": "Job Description:\nQualifications:\nOnly candidates with MS/ Ph.D. in A.I./M.L. with exposure to application on formal Methods and Verification\nJob Description - Agentic A.I. Development for Systems Engineering\nWe are looking for an AI Intern to develop a framework using A.I. to transform unstructured heuristic approach to structured Agentic approach based on certain pre-defined criteria. Test this structured approach on identified Systems of Interest for a specified workflow and deliverable..\nThis role combines systems thinking, logical thinking, software architecture, requirements engineering, Verification & Validation techniques with AI to accelerate innovation through A.I. driven software development in the aerospace industry.\nThis is a great opportunity for a candidate who wants to gain hands-on experience in digital transformation initiatives while contributing to meaningful business outcomes.\nIdeally, this is a 6 months internship and it should start in January 2027(date subject to flexibility).\nKey Responsibilities\nCore Technical Functions\n\u2022 Develop AI models to create structured agentic workflows by understanding existing ways of working\n\u2022 Develop tools that can adopt formal methods and test them on existing ways of working\n\u2022 Conduct studies on how teams in Airbus operate the methods, collect their needs and develop the tool that can handle multiple standards and evaluation criteria.\nImplementation & Collaboration\n\u2022 Partner with cross-functional teams to translate software requirements into technical solutions.\nRequired Skills and Expertise\n\u2022 Knowledge on AI\n\u2022 Software development\n\u2022 Communication and teamwork for translating business needs into technical solutions.\nThis job requires an awareness of any potential compliance risks and a commitment to act with integrity, as the foundation for the Company\u2019s success, reputation and sustainable growth.\nCompany:\nAirbus India Private Limited\nEmployment Type:\nInternship -------\nExperience Level:\nStudent\nJob Family:\nSupport to Management\nBy submitting your CV or application you are consenting to Airbus using and storing information about you for monitoring purposes relating to your application or future employment. This information will only be used by Airbus.\nAirbus is committed to achieving workforce diversity and creating an inclusive working environment. We welcome all applications irrespective of social and cultural background, age, gender, disability, sexual orientation or religious belief.\nAirbus is, and always has been, committed to equal opportunities for all. As such, we will never ask for any type of monetary exchange in the frame of a recruitment process. Any impersonation of Airbus to do so should be reported to emsom@airbus.com .\nAt Airbus, we support you to work, connect and collaborate more easily and flexibly. Wherever possible, we foster flexible working arrangements to stimulate innovative thinking.",
