    "apply_url": "https://jobs.lever.co/paytm/426a6834-1397-4e65-94af-69874c790805",
    "description": "About Paytm\nPaytm is India's leading mobile payments and financial services distribution company. Pioneer of the mobile QR payments revolution in India, Paytm builds technologies that help small businesses with payments and commerce.Paytm's mission is to serve half a billion Indians and bring them to the mainstream economy with the help of technology.\n\n\nJob Title\nTalent Acquisition Intern \u2013 Non-Tech Recruitment\n\nAbout the Role\nAs a Talent Acquisition Intern (Non-Tech), you will play an active role in driving talent identification and engagement across Paytm\u2019s business, sales, operations, and corporate functions. Working closely with recruiters and business stakeholders, you will help source, screen, and coordinate candidates to fuel Paytm\u2019s fast-paced growth.\nThis role is ideal for a proactive, energetic individual with strong communication skills, high learning agility, and an interest in modern, technology-enabled hiring practices. You will gain hands-on experience in end-to-end recruitment operations and candidate management in a high-volume fintech ecosystem.\n\nKey Responsibilities\nCandidate Sourcing: Leverage job boards, social channels, campus databases, and internal platforms to source qualified candidates for business, sales, and enabling function roles.\nScreening & Assessment: Conduct initial resume screening and phone evaluations to assess candidate suitability, communication skills, and role alignment.\nInterview Coordination: Manage end-to-end scheduling of interviews, candidate communications, and logistics to ensure a seamless candidate experience.\nPipeline Management: Maintain accurate candidate data and application stages across the Applicant Tracking System (ATS) and internal recruitment trackers.\nMarket Research: Perform basic market mapping and talent research to support recruiter search strategies for specialized non-tech profiles.\nProcess Automation & AI Adoption: Utilize modern sourcing tools, AI prompts, and automated communication platforms to speed up top-of-funnel hiring workflows.\n\nRequired Qualifications\nPursuing or recently completed a Bachelor\u2019s or Master\u2019s degree (MBA/PGDM in Human Resources or related fields preferred).\nStrong written and verbal communication skills with an ability to engage candidates professionally.\nExcellent organizational skills and attention to detail when managing multiple calendars and candidate pipelines.\nHigh learning agility, curiosity, and comfort working in a fast-paced environment.\nBasic proficiency in MS Office / Google Workspace (Sheets, Docs, Slides).\nPreferred Qualifications\nPrior internship experience in HR, recruitment, candidate sourcing, or talent coordination.\nFamiliarity with Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS) and professional networking platforms like LinkedIn.\nInterest in fintech, internet platforms, or high-growth technology environments.\n\nAI Expectations\nSourcing & Search: Practical use of modern search methodologies and basic AI tools/prompts to quickly discover candidate profiles and boolean search strings.\nCommunication: Utilizing AI tools for drafting personalized candidate outreach messages, interview invitations, and follow-ups.\nProductivity: Leveraging AI-driven tools and automation to summarize profiles, reduce administrative turnaround time, and improve daily recruitment throughput.\n\nIdeal Candidate\nDemonstrates Ownership & Bias for Action by taking initiative on daily sourcing and coordination tasks.\nExhibits Learning Agility with an eagerness to absorb recruiting best practices and stay open to new tools and ideas.\nDisplays Speed of Execution and adaptability in managing tight hiring schedules and candidate communication.\nStrong focus on Candidate Experience and professional ethics.\n",
