    "id": 120,
    "normalized_key": "gehealthcare:researchinternai:bangalore",
    "title": "Research Intern - AI",
    "company": "GE HealthCare",
    "location_raw": "IND19-01-Bengaluru-EPIP 122 (Phase II)",
    "city": "Bangalore",
    "job_type": "internship",
    "posted_date": "2026-08-31T23:59:59+00:00",
    "apply_url": "https://gehc.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/GEHC_ExternalSite/job/IND19-01-Bengaluru-EPIP-122-Phase-II/Research-Intern---AI_R4043882-1",
    "description": "Job Description Summary\nAs a Research intern \u2013 AI, you will collaboratively execute technology programs in development and research of AI algorithms for improving medical workflows. You will interact with technologists and engineers to develop and deliver novel solutions for complex, multi-disciplinary problems for GE Healthcare.\nGE HealthCare is a leading global medical technology and digital solutions innovator. Our purpose is to create a world where healthcare has no limits. Unlock your ambition, turn ideas into world-changing realities, and join an organization where every voice makes a difference, and every difference builds a healthier world.\nJob Description\nRoles and Responsibilities\n\u2022 Specific areas of required expertise are: Image analytics, Deep Learning, Inverse problems in Imaging, Clinical decisioning, super resolution reconstruction.\n\u2022 Expertise in Deep Learning and Computer Vision/ Image processing, TensorFlow, Pytorch and Keras is required.\n\u2022 Experience with Generative AI techniques including diffusion models, GANs, foundation vision models, multimodal models, and large language models (LLMs).\n\u2022 Experience applying generative AI to medical imaging use cases such as image synthesis, image reconstruction, report generation, data augmentation, segmentation, and clinical workflow automation.\n\u2022 Familiarity with vision-language models (VLMs), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and multimodal AI systems for healthcare applications.\nRequired Qualification\n\u2022 Currently pursuing a PhD in Computer Science / Data Sciences / AI from a reputed institute\n\u2022 Understanding of building large scale AI such as generative AI models, large vision/language models, and multi-modal AI models for problems related to segmentation, detection, quantification, measurements, classification, etc.\n\u2022 Implementation experience with a variety of high-level languages (e.g. Python, C++)\n\u2022 Staying current on published state-of-the-art algorithms and competing technologies.\n\u2022 Experience and demonstrated capability to handle challenges with vague or abstract problem definition.\n\u2022 Experience with frameworks and tools such as Keras, HuggingFace, Vector databases, PyTorch, Tensorflow etc.\n\u2022 Experience working with large scale AI training.\n\u2022 An in-depth understanding of machine learning algorithms and modeling (e.g., semi-supervised or weakly supervised learning, generative models, transfer learning, optimization, large language models, etc.)\n\u2022 Ability to work independently and as a team player\nInclusion and Diversity\nGE Healthcare is an Equal Opportunity Employer where inclusion matters. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law.\nWe expect all employees to live and breathe our behaviors: to act with humility and build trust; lead with transparency; deliver with focus, and drive ownership \u2013 always with unyielding integrity.\nOur total rewards are designed to unlock your ambition by giving you the boost and flexibility you need to turn your ideas into world-changing realities. Our salary and benefits are everything you\u2019d expect from an organization with global strength and scale, and you\u2019ll be surrounded by career opportunities in a culture that fosters care, collaboration and support.\nAdditional Information\nRelocation Assistance Provided: Yes",
