    "id": 142,
    "normalized_key": "nasdaq:analystinformationdevelopertechnicalwriter:mumbai",
    "title": "Analyst\u2014Information Developer / Technical Writer",
    "company": "Nasdaq",
    "location_raw": "India - Mumbai - Maharashtra",
    "city": "Mumbai",
    "job_type": "job",
    "posted_date": "2026-06-11T23:59:59+00:00",
    "apply_url": "https://nasdaq.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Global_External_Site/job/India---Mumbai---Maharashtra/Analyst-Information-Developer---Technical-Writer_R0026109",
    "description": "Nasdaq Technology is looking for a passionate Information Developer Analyst with focus on Technical Writing and Help Center Release Management, to join the Mumbai technology center in India. If innovation and efficiency drive you forward, this is the place for you!\nNasdaq is continuously revolutionizing markets and undergoing transformations while we adopt new technologies to develop innovative solutions, constantly striving to rewrite tomorrow. As an Information Developer Analyst, you will focus on Help Center release management for Eqlipse products\u2014publishing Help Centers using established processes, guided experted team members, ensuring product information is updated, built, and published accurately. This role is foundational, building product knowledge needed for broader responsibilities over time.\nWe are looking for candidates with a genuine desire and drive to deliver top technology solutions to today's markets.\nWith this position we offer\nJoin the Information Development organization, a global team driving the digitalization of product information and growing the use of Help Centers, continuously improving how customers learn, adopt, and operate Nasdaq Eqlipse products \u2014 mission-critical solutions delivered to financial market infrastructure organizations, including exchanges and clearing houses.\nRole Responsibilities\nAs an Information Developer , your focus will be developing and publishing product information to modern Help Centers. Besides working closely with your colleagues in Sweden, you will also work closely with Nasdaq teams in other countries.\n\u2022 Plan, coordinate, and publish product information for Help Center releases.\n\u2022 Collaborate with developers, business analysts, and project managers.\n\u2022 Ensure release information is clear, accurate, and delivered on time.\n\u2022 Build understanding of how software changes affect business and technical users.\n\u2022 Contribute to a consistent and high-quality release experience for customers.\nWe expect you to have:\n\u2022 Excellent written and spoken English.\n\u2022 Strong attention to detail and structured way of working.\n\u2022 Genuine interest in communication, software, and process-oriented work.\n\u2022 Ability to learn quickly and follow defined procedures with accuracy.\n\u2022 Strong collaboration skills and a team-first mindset.\n\u2022 Curiousity to understand complex products and turn technical input into useful customer-facing information.\n\u2022 Education Qualification: Engineering degree or equivalent technical education.\nIt would be great if you\n\u2022 Internship or early professional experience in software, product documentation, or business/technical analysis.\n\u2022 Exposure to agile ways of working.\n\u2022 Interest in financial markets.\n\u2022 Experience with structured content, XML-based authoring tools such as MadCap Flare, Jira, or similar tools.\nDoes it sound like you?\nAs the selection process is ongoing, please submit your application in English as soon as possible. We will get back to you in 2-3 weeks.\nCome as you are\nNasdaq is an equal opportunity employer. We positively encourage applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates regardless of age, color, disability, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, veteran status, genetic information or any other status protected by applicable law.\nNasdaq is a leading global provider of trading, clearing, exchange technology, listing, information, and public company services. As the creator of the world's first electronic stock market, its technology powers more than 100 marketplaces in 50 countries. Nasdaq is home to over 4,000 total listings with a market value of approximately $12 trillion.\nTo learn more, about our business visit business.nasdaq.com. Check out more about our Life at Nasdaq.\nCome as You Are\nNasdaq is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds and identities.\nWe are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where diverse perspectives, experiences, and identities are valued and celebrated.\nWe ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided with reasonable accommodation throughout the hiring process.",
